#23536
The Ocean~
  You now lay in the heart of a tight-woven fabric of seaweed 
that seems to stretch to the ends of the universe. The landscape
that presents itself is something like a dream, a single 
unbroken carpet of a trillion knotted strands, it surface pulsing,
twitching, throbbing, trembling, and its colors shifting everywhere
through a restless spectrum of deep assertive tones.
~
