#23565
A Sloping Shoreline~
   Out of the ocean fog rises a long shoreline, stretching far south. Unsure
of your exact location, you decide to go ashore. The shoreline is quite
rocky, and rises to a widening plains to the east. A large trail leads
eastward, and judging by the tracks of shodden hooves and cartwheels, it
was travelled by a large party within the last week or so. A stiff ocean
breeze blows from the west, crashing large waves into the banks.
~
